This product includes software developed by third parties:

- AndroidLiquidGlass / Backdrop and Shapes by Kyant (Apache-2.0), including UI components
  adapted from its catalog app (ui/glass). https://github.com/Kyant0/AndroidLiquidGlass
- Oboe by Google (Apache-2.0). https://github.com/google/oboe
- dr_libs (dr_wav, dr_flac, dr_mp3) by David Reid (public domain / MIT-0). https://github.com/mackron/dr_libs
- stb_vorbis by Sean Barrett (public domain / MIT). https://github.com/nothings/stb
- AndroidX, Jetpack Compose and Kotlin coroutines (Apache-2.0).
- youtubedl-android by yausername and junkfood02 (GPL-3.0), which bundles yt-dlp (Unlicense), CPython (PSF), FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) and QuickJS (MIT). https://github.com/yausername/youtubedl-android
- NewPipeExtractor by the NewPipe team (GPL-3.0). https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipeExtractor
- OkHttp (Apache-2.0).
- PO token generation (BotGuard in a WebView, assets/po_token.html and download/BotGuard.kt) is ported from NewPipe (GPL-3.0). https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipe

Because the release APK bundles GPL-3.0 components (youtubedl-android and NewPipeExtractor), the APK as a whole is distributed under the terms of the GPL-3.0. The source code written for OpenSoundboard stays under Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE); the complete corresponding source of every release is this repository at the release tag.

